{"title":"2023 WSMO Team Round Problems/Problem 14","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_WSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> with circumcircle centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Given <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/8/068be3f100d60868052abb7b3b1a43edd8e8e1b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=2&lt;CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"118\" height=\"15\" />, the circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/3/e23bfc5d0d1ec23144c1b81e7d56228d374e8ee9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{ABO}$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> is tangent to the circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/b/d5bf8f2ada0e5bce0f28807c0c16d856bf57c697.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{COD}$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />. The circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/8/478e065cc4f0cf4d06f0b4ea307082ada018a0be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{AOD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> passes through the center of the circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/3/e23bfc5d0d1ec23144c1b81e7d56228d374e8ee9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{ABO}$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" />. Given the radius of the circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the area and perimeter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />, respectively. The value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/b/adb36a075731cab8ae1a204133e352697129f810.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{A}{P}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"39\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/c/11c5ea5774a663fa2517dce85e6d24f66d60f0c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a\\sqrt{b}}{c}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"35\" height=\"41\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is a squarefree positive integer and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/a/eaa540ef6360899066bc4fd5b466f10a3bc55a93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"25\" height=\"11\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/b/6ebd1e0356cfe09c0d9b5459d6f1542657bb5891.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_WSMO_Team_Round_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<center> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/9/729c95903d3248128b504f2f4de12b34fd061d13.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(250); pair O = (0,0); pair O1 = (0,-18/sqrt(35)); pair O3 = (0,81*sqrt(35)/140); pair O4 = (-9,-9/sqrt(35)); pair A = (-1,-sqrt(35)); pair B = (1,-sqrt(35)); pair C = (26/9,8sqrt(35)/9); pair D = (-26/9,8sqrt(35)/9);  label(&quot;$A$&quot;, (A.x,A.y-0.2), S); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, S); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, NE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;, (D.x,D.y+0.3), N); label(&quot;$O$&quot;, O, NE); label(&quot;$O_1$&quot;, O1, SE); label(&quot;$O_3$&quot;, O3, NE);; draw(O3--O--O1, dotted+linewidth(1.2));  draw(circle(O,6),blue); draw(circle(O1,O1.y),red); draw(circle(O3,O3.y),red); draw(arc(O4,54/sqrt(35),-50,60),heavygreen+dotted+linewidth(2)); draw(A--B--C--D--cycle,black+linewidth(1.2));  draw(A--O,dotted+linewidth(1)); draw(A--O1,dotted+linewidth(1)); draw(D--O,dotted+linewidth(1));  dot(O); dot(O1); dot(O3); [/asy]\" width=\"325\" height=\"418\" /> </center><p> Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/b/43b6f63aa2266ef1b39b31386bd17b28e25faaac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/1/3216e8846eb44f1055c322fb5bd30169d5d62cec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> be the circumcenters of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/9/4097e707215c7c2085c3fd539de4c228d44f1880.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$COD$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/0/890bd5d40a42153edcb992ad0a14cac52ca2eaf8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABO$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />, respectively. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/0/890bd5d40a42153edcb992ad0a14cac52ca2eaf8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABO$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/9/4097e707215c7c2085c3fd539de4c228d44f1880.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$COD$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> share point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, they must be externally tangent at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, meaning <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/b/43b6f63aa2266ef1b39b31386bd17b28e25faaac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/1/3216e8846eb44f1055c322fb5bd30169d5d62cec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> are collinear. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/1/9519849ff165264c55d06af36c5d030a98b6d066.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AO=BO$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/6/4561262a4ac359d12bc94e5e0b4beb047b189ebc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CO=DO$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"85\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/0/890bd5d40a42153edcb992ad0a14cac52ca2eaf8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABO$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/9/4097e707215c7c2085c3fd539de4c228d44f1880.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$COD$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> are isosceles, meaning <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/2/572a9b194f842c6e7eba2c2a3385ead2f132199f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OO_1\\perp AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"90\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/4/284f5cbf3e68d768283c6fddd163ed17ae56ed2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OO_3\\perp CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"92\" height=\"17\" />. From the fact that that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/7/a8746041676f935bb4a7ffa6c1327e3c19779bf8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_3,O,O_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"18\" /> are collinear, this directly implies that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/e/89ee5420004c3b2a8f1f0cf81594b54dbbb1da5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB\\parallel CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"19\" />, meaning <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is an isosceles trapezoid. Now, the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />-height of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/0/890bd5d40a42153edcb992ad0a14cac52ca2eaf8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABO$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> is of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/a/bca602205e9520ffefb8817432b9e1288342208d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{6^2-\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)^2}=\\sqrt{35}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"163\" height=\"56\" />. So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/e/b0e5a46c1f239476002f67e133311127d78619e9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[OO_1=\\frac{(OA)(AB)(BO)}{4[ABO]}=\\frac{6\\cdot2\\cdot6}{4\\cdot\\frac{2\\cdot\\sqrt{35}}{2}}=\\frac{18}{\\sqrt{35}}.\\]\" width=\"345\" height=\"48\" /> Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/a/a1a9174fd9c0ce03fe3bbad8e4d3cb4f3a3e3f01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta=\\angle OAO_1=\\angle AOO_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"184\" height=\"17\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/c/eac95145b40636668dd93313a099b771388d9a8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OO_1A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"17\" /> is isosceles, have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/4/bb4eb92d88fbef4ac1f7c8d7688bd9964f3cc277.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos\\theta=\\frac{\\frac{OA}{2}}{O_1A}=\\frac{3}{\\frac{18}{\\sqrt{35}}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{35}}{6}\\implies\\sin\\theta=\\sqrt{1-\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{35}}{6}\\right)^2}=\\frac{1}{6}.\\]\" width=\"489\" height=\"63\" /> Now, from angle chasing, we have  \\begin{align*} \\angle OO_1A = 180-2\\theta\\quad&amp;\\text{since }OO_1A\\text{ is isosceles,}\\\\ \\angle ODA=180-\\angle{OO_1A}=2\\theta\\quad&amp;\\text{since }ODAO_1\\text{ is cyclic,}\\\\ \\angle OAD=\\angle ODA=2\\theta\\quad&amp;\\text{since }AOD\\text{ is isosceles,}\\\\ \\angle AOB=2\\angle AOO_1=2\\theta\\quad&amp;\\text{from symmetry,}\\\\ \\angle OAB=\\frac{180-\\angle AOB}{2}=90-\\theta\\quad&amp;\\text{since }ABO\\text{ is isosceles,}\\\\ \\angle DAB=\\angle DAO+\\angle OAB=2\\theta+(90-\\theta)=90+\\theta)\\quad&amp;\\text{, and }\\\\ \\angle CDA=180-\\angle DAB = 90-\\theta\\quad&amp;\\text{since }AB\\parallel CD. \\end{align*} Now, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/0922c3300b6fd7973836d0ae3a473edaf8e909b9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sin OAD=\\sin(2\\theta)=2\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta=2\\left(\\frac{1}{6}\\right)\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{35}}{6}\\right)=\\frac{\\sqrt{35}}{18}\\quad\\text{and}\\]\" width=\"506\" height=\"53\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/1/ee11c8c788ce96cef0e383029bc3674dea890ac4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos(2\\theta)=\\sqrt{1-\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{35}}{18}\\right)^2}=\\frac{17}{18}.\\]\" width=\"253\" height=\"63\" /> We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/6/5e61be9647c18812ce578718af04358907e83c1f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AD = 2\\cdot(AO\\cos\\angle OAD)=12\\cdot\\cos(2\\theta)=12\\cdot\\frac{17}{18}=\\frac{34}{3}.\\]\" width=\"444\" height=\"38\" /> Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is an isosceles trapezoid, this means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/6/7564c0342c90d187b8cfae8cdd8cf939619973b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CB=\\frac{34}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"77\" height=\"38\" /> as well. Now,  \\begin{align*} CD&amp;=AB+2AD\\cos(\\angle CDA)=2+2AD\\cos(90-\\theta)\\\\ &amp;=2+2AD\\sin\\theta=2+2\\left(\\frac{34}{3}\\right)\\left(\\frac{1}{6}\\right)=\\frac{52}{9}. \\end{align*} This gives us a perimeter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/c/67c13931136ec2eb52c2cd637771b373f2853db9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[N=AB+BC+CD+DA=2+\\frac{34}{3}+\\frac{52}{9}+\\frac{34}{3}=\\frac{274}{9}\\]\" width=\"443\" height=\"38\" /> and an area of  \\begin{align*} M&amp;=\\left(\\frac{AB+CD}{2}\\right)\\left(AD\\sin\\angle CDA\\right)\\\\ &amp;=\\left(\\frac{2+\\frac{52}{9}}{2}\\right)\\left(\\frac{34}{3}\\sin(90-\\theta)\\right)\\\\ &amp;=\\frac{35}{9}\\cdot\\frac{34}{3}\\cdot\\cos\\theta\\\\ &amp;=\\frac{35}{9}\\cdot\\frac{34}{3}\\cdot\\frac{\\sqrt{35}}{6}\\\\ &amp;=\\frac{595\\sqrt{35}}{81}. \\end{align*} So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/c/c2cbf24facbb2d66c6ccfa7e9de449b9b0462259.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{M}{N}=\\frac{\\frac{595\\sqrt{35}}{81}}{\\frac{274}{9}}=\\frac{595\\sqrt{35}}{2466}\\implies 595+35+2466=\\boxed{3096}.\\]\" width=\"437\" height=\"50\" />\n</p><p>~pinkpig\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018024413\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.017 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.025 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 195/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 10320/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:31926:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018024413 and revision id 274655. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}